${fileList}
Engine reference: ${ROOT}/docs/engine-reference/godot/ (VERSION.md, breaking-changes.md, deprecated-apis.md, current-best-practices.md, modules/). For each ADR: (1) is the approach idiomatic for 4.7.2; (2) any API or pattern deprecated, changed after your training cutoff, or simply wrong (wrong signatures, things that will not compile, e.g. const of constructed objects, packed arrays passed by reference, typed-return override rule 4.7, member names clashing with Object methods); (3) engine gotchas the draft misses. Be concrete and give a confidence per claim. You may probe facts headless with "C:/Users/dasbl/Documents/Godot/Godot_v4.7.2-stable_mono_win64_console.exe" --headless --script <file> from a scratch dir OUTSIDE the repo (C:/Users/dasbl/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/adr-probes/engine-review/). Also flag engine-level contradictions BETWEEN the ADRs in cross_adr. Return findings per ADR with ids E1, E2... (blocking=true for wrong API / will not compile / incompatible), each with a concrete amendment; cross_adr items with an owner_adr that should change.`,
    { label: 'review:engine', phase: 'Review', schema: REVIEW_SCHEMA, model: 'sonnet', effort: 'high', agentType: 'godot-specialist' }),
  () => agent(`Review-only task: do NOT edit or write any file. Run gate TD-ADR (definition and verdict format: ${ROOT}/.claude/docs/director-gates/td-adr.md) on EACH of these six newly drafted, parallel-authored Foundation ADRs (Proposed, Godot 4.7.2, GDScript, review mode full), AND review them as a set for cross-ADR coherence, because their authors could not see each other's drafts:
${fileList}
Authors' stated assumptions about each other:
${assumptions}
Binding context: ${ROOT}/docs/registry/architecture.yaml; already-written Proposed ADRs ADR-0001, 0002, 0003 and ADR-0007 in ${ROOT}/docs/architecture/; ${ROOT}/docs/architecture/architecture.md (System Layer Map, Data Flow, Required ADRs, Spikes, Open Questions); TR rows in docs/architecture/tr-baseline.md. Read docs by section (grep headings, bounded reads).
For each ADR: verdict APPROVE / CONCERNS / REJECT with findings T1, T2... (severity, blocking true when it must change before Accept, concrete amendment). Check: contradictions with registry stances and ADR-0001/2/3/7; scope overlap or gaps between the six (who owns what); right-sizing for a solo/small-team MVP; traceability of the ADR's TR rows; spike gating stated honestly. In cross_adr list every inconsistency between two or more of the six (e.g. dirty-key layout vs notification vs subscriber contract; canonical encoding vs save container vs ADR-0007 hash input; lint ownership in ADR-0010 vs rules other ADRs assign to it; fault-domain usage), with the single owner_adr that should change and the exact amendment.`,
