(1) Append these registry candidates to docs/registry/architecture.yaml. Follow the file's header LAYOUT rules exactly (block lists, dash at column 2, fields two columns past the dash, quote values containing ": "). Before each edit read the current file; append each new entry AFTER the last existing entry of its section (state_ownership, interfaces, performance_budgets, api_decisions, forbidden_patterns), before that section's "# Example:" comment block. For section referenced_by_update, add the ADR path to the named existing entry's referenced_by list only. Never modify or delete other existing fields. Skip a candidate that duplicates an existing entry name or another candidate (merge into one entry instead, listing both ADRs in referenced_by) and report it. Then run: bash .claude/scripts/registry.sh validate  and also  python -c "import yaml;yaml.safe_load(open('docs/registry/architecture.yaml',encoding='utf-8'))"  and fix any layout error you introduced.
Candidates: ${JSON.stringify(candidates)}
(2) Append to production/session-logs/decision-log.md (append only, never rewrite) one section per ADR in the existing format: "## 2026-10-28 — architecture-decision (ADR-NNNN, foundation-adrs workflow)" then for each decision "**Decision point:** ... / **Options considered:** ... / **Chosen:** ... / **Reason:** ... / **Category:** architecture", plus one entry for the joint review ("Revise flagged items", applied ids, declined ids with reasons) and one for the registry update.
Decisions: ${JSON.stringify(decisions)}
Do not edit any other file. Never commit. Return a short plain-text report: entries added per section, merged duplicates, validate output, decision-log sections appended.`,
  { label: 'registry+log', phase: 'Registry', model: 'sonnet', effort: 'medium' })

return {
  authored: authored.map(r => ({ adr: r.adr_id, path: r.path, summary: r.summary, depends_on: r.depends_on })),
  verdicts: {
    engine: engine ? engine.reviews.map(x => ({ adr: x.adr_id, verdict: x.verdict, blocking: x.findings.filter(f => f.blocking).length, total: x.findings.length })) : null,
    td: td ? td.reviews.map(x => ({ adr: x.adr_id, verdict: x.verdict, blocking: x.findings.filter(f => f.blocking).length, total: x.findings.length })) : null,
    cross_adr_count: (engine ? engine.cross_adr.length : 0) + (td ? td.cross_adr.length : 0),
  },
  revised: revised.map(r => ({ adr: r.adr_id, applied: r.applied.length, declined: r.declined, open_questions: r.open_questions })),
  gdd_sync: revised.map(r => ({ adr: r.adr_id, items: r.gdd_sync })),
  confirm,
  registryReport,
}

